{"book":"fractions","bookTitle":"Fractions","concept":8,"title":"Multiplying fractions","grades":"Grade 7","goal":"I can multiply fractions and find a fraction of an amount.","teach":"Multiply the numerators, then multiply the denominators. Simplify before or after. The word “of” means multiply. Change mixed numbers to improper fractions first. Multiplying by a fraction smaller than 1 makes the amount smaller.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:138px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 106 132\"><rect x=\"1.0\" y=\"1.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"27.0\" y=\"1.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"53.0\" y=\"1.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"79.0\" y=\"1.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"1.0\" y=\"27.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"27.0\" y=\"27.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"53.0\" y=\"27.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"79.0\" y=\"27.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"1.0\" y=\"53.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"27.0\" y=\"53.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"53.0\" y=\"53.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"79.0\" y=\"53.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"1.0\" y=\"79.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"27.0\" y=\"79.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"53.0\" y=\"79.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"79.0\" y=\"79.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"1.0\" y=\"105.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"27.0\" y=\"105.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"53.0\" y=\"105.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"79.0\" y=\"105.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"26.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">3 of 4 columns and 2 of 5 rows: they overlap in 6 of 20 cells, so <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span> × <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">6</span><span class=\"d\">20</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span>.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Calculate <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span> × <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span>.","steps":["Multiply the numerators: 3 × 2 = 6.","Multiply the denominators: 4 × 5 = 20.","Simplify: <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">6</span><span class=\"d\">20</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span>."]},"watch":"Multiplying does not always make a number bigger. Half of 8 is 4.","qs":[{"text":"Thandi’s muffin recipe needs <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span> cup of sugar. She makes <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">3</span></span> of the recipe. How much sugar does she need?","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Cups of sugar","a":"1/2","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"“Two thirds of” means multiply by two thirds.","steps":"1. Rule: “of” means ×. To find <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"d\">b</span></span> of an amount, divide by b, then multiply by a.<br>2. <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">3</span></span> of <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">3</span></span> × <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span><br>3. Formula: <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"d\">b</span></span> × <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"d\">d</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a × c</span><span class=\"d\">b × d</span></span>. Multiply the numerators, multiply the denominators, then simplify.<br>4. = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">6</span><span class=\"d\">12</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> cup"},{"text":"Calculate <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> × <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">7</span></span>.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":"Answer"}],"hint":"Multiply the tops, multiply the bottoms.","steps":"1. Formula: <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"d\">b</span></span> × <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"d\">d</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a × c</span><span class=\"d\">b × d</span></span>.<br>2. Multiply the numerators: 1 × 3 = 3.<br>3. Multiply the denominators: 2 × 7 = 14.<br>4. Answer: <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">14</span></span>."},{"text":"Calculate <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">4</span><span class=\"d\">9</span></span> × <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">8</span></span>.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":"Answer"}],"hint":"Multiply, then look for a common factor to simplify.","steps":"1. Formula: <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"d\">b</span></span> × <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"d\">d</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a × c</span><span class=\"d\">b × d</span></span>. Multiply the numerators, multiply the denominators, then simplify.<br>2. <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">4</span><span class=\"d\">9</span></span> × <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">8</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">4 × 3</span><span class=\"d\">9 × 8</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">12</span><span class=\"d\">72</span></span><br>3. = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">6</span></span>"}]}